{
  "raw": {
    "http://jobs.shu.edu/cw/en-us/job/497519/assistant-professor-of-classics": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Classics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Classics Apply now Job no: 497519 Full time/Part time: Full-time Location: South Orange Categories: Faculty The Department of Languages, Literatures and Cultures at Seton Hall University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Classics at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning in the Fall of 2027. We seek a dynamic scholar and dedicated teacher with a strong record of scholarly achievement and demonstrated excellence in undergraduate education. The successful candidate will have broad expertise in the field of Classics and be prepared to teach both Greek and Latin at a range of levels, from introductory through advanced courses, as well as elective courses of interest to a general student population and courses within the University Core and the Honors Program. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research and teaching engage creatively with the classical world and who can contribute to the intellectual vitality and curricular development of our undergraduate program. Candidates should demonstrate an active and promising program of research, as evidenced by publications, scholarly presentations, and/or other significant contributions to the field. We welcome applicants working in any area of Classics, including but not limited to Greek and Roman literature, history, culture, archaeology, religion, philosophy, reception studies, or the classical tradition. Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will also demonstrate a strong record of teaching excellence and a commitment to innovative, student-centered pedagogy. In addition to teaching courses in Greek and Latin language and literature, the candidate will be expected to develop innovative and engaging undergraduate courses that expand the study of the ancient Mediterranean world and connect Classics with broader intellectual, cultural, and contemporary concerns. We especially welcome candidates who can contribute to interdisciplinary teaching and who are interested in developing courses that attract students from across the university. Finally, as the director of the Classics Program, the successful candidate will be expected to engage in creative program building activities that engage students and faculty across campus. Required Qualifications: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Classics or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Candidates should demonstrate: •A strong record of, or clear potential for, scholarly excellence and publication; •Demonstrated excellence in undergraduate teaching; •Advanced proficiency in both Ancient Greek and Latin; •The ability to teach Greek and Latin language and literature at multiple levels; •A commitment to innovative and inclusive approaches to undergraduate education; •The ability to develop new courses that engage students with Classics from interdisciplinary and/or contemporary perspectives. Salary Range: $59,091-$65,657 Exempt/Nonexempt: Exempt Physical Demands: General Office Environment Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, research statement, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and three letters of recommendation Benefits Information: Full Time Benefits Life today is complex. That’s why Seton Hall University offers a comprehensive package of benefits and programs to help you simplify and enrich your life. These benefits are important elements of your total university compensation package. Benefits include but are not limited to bundled medical, prescription, and vision insurance, dental insurance, and life insurance, and retirement plan. More information is available at https://www.shu.edu/human-resources/benefits.html . Seton Hall University is located in South Orange, New Jersey, 14 miles from New York City. It is the oldest Catholic diocesan institution of higher education in the United States and is home to about 6,300 undergraduate and 3,700 graduate students. A vibrant and culturally inclusive community, Seton Hall pursues academic excellence and ethical development in a collaborative environment and prepares its students to be servant leaders in their professional and community lives. Seton Hall University is an equal opportunity employer. It honors diverse perspectives and welcomes employees from all faith traditions. In turn, its employees respect Catholic beliefs and values, engage in servant leadership, and support the University’s mission as a Catholic institution of higher education. Advertised: 14 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "http://jobs.shu.edu/cw/en-us/job/497510/associate-professor-school-of-law": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, School of Law",
      "description": "Associate Professor, School of Law Apply now Job no: 497510 Full time/Part time: Full-time Location: Newark Categories: Faculty Seton Hall University School of Law welcomes applications for a tenure-track position to begin July 1, 2027. Candidates should demonstrate (i) scholarly promise, (ii) the ability or potential to be an outstanding teacher and mentor who can prepare students for the practice of law, and (iii) leadership in service toward building an equitable and diverse academic community. We will consider entry-level and lateral candidates. We have particular teaching needs in tax law. Duties and Responsibilities: Seton Hall Law School offers a vibrant, energetic academic environment. Located in downtown Newark, New Jersey, approximately 20 minutes from Manhattan, Seton Hall Law is especially well-regarded in the health and life sciences law, intellectual property, cybersecurity, and privacy arenas, and it is in the process of expanding its role in energy, gaming/sports, technology and data analytics. The main campus of Seton Hall University is located in South Orange, New Jersey, about 4 miles from the Law School . Seton Hall University is the oldest Catholic diocesan institution of higher education in the United States and is home to about 6,300 undergraduate and 4,700 graduate students. A vibrant and culturally diverse community, Seton Hall pursues academic excellence and ethical development in a collaborative environment and prepares its students to be servant leaders in their professional and community lives. Seton Hall University is an Equal Opportunity employer. It honors diversity and respects the religious commitments of all its employees. In turn, its employees respect Catholic beliefs and values, engage the Catholic Intellectual Tradition, and support the university’s mission as a Catholic institution of higher education. Required Qualifications: Candidates must have a J.D. or equivalent degree and a record of academic excellence. Salary Range: $153,855-$170,951 Exempt/Nonexempt: Exempt Physical Demands: General Office Environment Special Instructions to Applicants: The following documents should be uploaded with your application: CV (with references), cover letter, scholarly agenda, and job talk paper (or abstract with expected date for completion of the draft). Benefits Information: Full Time Benefits Life today is complex. That’s why Seton Hall University offers a comprehensive package of benefits and programs to help you simplify and enrich your life. These benefits are important elements of your total university compensation package. Benefits include but are not limited to bundled medical, prescription, and vision insurance, dental insurance, and life insurance, and retirement plan. More information is available at https://www.shu.edu/human-resources/benefits.html . Seton Hall University is located in South Orange, New Jersey, 14 miles from New York City. It is the oldest Catholic diocesan institution of higher education in the United States and is home to about 6,300 undergraduate and 3,700 graduate students. A vibrant and culturally inclusive community, Seton Hall pursues academic excellence and ethical development in a collaborative environment and prepares its students to be servant leaders in their professional and community lives. Seton Hall University is an equal opportunity employer. It honors diverse perspectives and welcomes employees from all faith traditions. In turn, its employees respect Catholic beliefs and values, engage in servant leadership, and support the University’s mission as a Catholic institution of higher education. Advertised: 14 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
