    "http://jobs.shu.edu/cw/en-us/job/497495/practicum-director-master-of-social-work-program": {
      "title": "Practicum Director - Master of Social Work Program",
      "description": "Practicum Director - Master of Social Work Program Apply now Job no: 497495 Full time/Part time: Full-time Location: South Orange Categories: Faculty The Practicum Director provides leadership and administration for the MSW practicum education program while supporting student recruitment, admissions, enrollment, retention, and community partnerships. The Director ensures practicum operations align with MSW Program objectives, University policies, and applicable CSWE accreditation standards. Duties and Responsibilities: Practicum Administration Oversee all aspects of practicum education, including placement processes, policies, documentation, timelines, student evaluations, and program operations. Student Placement and Support Coordinate student placements from initial readiness assessment through placement confirmation and completion. Address placement challenges, student performance concerns, agency issues, and necessary remediation or placement changes. Agency and Community Partnerships Recruit, evaluate, and maintain a diverse network of high-quality practicum sites and qualified practicum instructors. Develop strategic partnerships with nonprofit, government, healthcare, educational, behavioral health, and community organizations. Practicum Instructor Support Orient and support practicum instructors regarding supervision expectations, student competencies, evaluations, University requirements, and professional standards. Compliance and Accreditation Maintain practicum records, affiliation agreements, assessment data, and processes necessary to support University requirements and CSWE accreditation. Participate in accreditation reporting, assessment, program review, and continuous improvement activities. Student Recruitment Participate actively in MSW recruitment through information sessions, open houses, recruitment events, community outreach, and prospective student engagement. Develop recruitment pipelines through universities, employers, alumni, community organizations, and practicum partners. Admissions and Application Review Participate in MSW admissions by reviewing applications, evaluating applicant readiness, conducting interviews when appropriate, and making admissions recommendations. Support Advanced Standing review, admitted-student outreach, and enrollment yield initiatives. Student Success and Retention Collaborate with program leadership and faculty to identify barriers to student progression and implement strategies supporting retention, professional development, and successful degree completion. Program and Partnership Development Represent the MSW Program with community organizations, professional associations, alumni, and prospective partners. Identify opportunities that strengthen practicum education, recruitment, employment pipelines, community engagement, and overall program growth. Administration and Supervision Supervise graduate assistants and practicum-related administrative support as assigned and oversee practicum management systems, student and agency records, and operational workflows. Required Qualifications: MSW from a CSWE-accredited program. Minimum two years of post-MSW social work practice experience. Strong administrative, organizational, communication, and relationship-building skills. Experience working with students, interns, supervisees, or emerging professionals. Ability to develop community partnerships and manage multiple priorities. Required teaching of 1 course per semester. Position Expectations The Practicum Director serves as an educational administrator and strategic partner responsible for strengthening practicum education, student recruitment, admissions, student success, community partnerships, and MSW Program growth. Local and regional travel for site development, recruitment, and community engagement is expected. Desired Qualifications: Experience in social work practicum/field education or higher education. Experience with student recruitment, graduate admissions, or enrollment. Experience with CSWE accreditation and program assessment. Experience with Tevera or a comparable practicum management system. Social work licensure preferred; advanced clinical licensure is not required solely by CSWE standards. PhD in Social Work, Public Administration, or a related field is preferred. Licenses and Certificates: LCSW Salary Range: $60,000-$72,000 Exempt/Nonexempt: Exempt Physical Demands: General Office Environment Special Instructions to Applicants: Benefits Information: Full Time Benefits Life today is complex. That’s why Seton Hall University offers a comprehensive package of benefits and programs to help you simplify and enrich your life. These benefits are important elements of your total university compensation package. Benefits include but are not limited to bundled medical, prescription, and vision insurance, dental insurance, and life insurance, and retirement plan. More information is available at https://www.shu.edu/human-resources/benefits.html . Seton Hall University is located in South Orange, New Jersey, 14 miles from New York City. It is the oldest Catholic diocesan institution of higher education in the United States and is home to about 6,300 undergraduate and 3,700 graduate students. A vibrant and culturally inclusive community, Seton Hall pursues academic excellence and ethical development in a collaborative environment and prepares its students to be servant leaders in their professional and community lives. Seton Hall University is an equal opportunity employer. It honors diverse perspectives and welcomes employees from all faith traditions. In turn, its employees respect Catholic beliefs and values, engage in servant leadership, and support the University’s mission as a Catholic institution of higher education. Advertised: 17 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "http://jobs.shu.edu/cw/en-us/job/497488/assistant-professor-of-computer-science": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Computer Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Computer Science Apply now Job no: 497488 Full time/Part time: Full-time Location: South Orange Categories: Faculty The Department of Mathematics and Computer Science at Seton Hall University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Computer Science. The appointment will begin in August 2027. Duties and Responsibilities: Preference will be given to candidates whose research expertise aligns with one or more of the following areas: cloud and edge computing, cyber-physical systems, and AI systems. Responsibilities include teaching computer science courses at all undergraduate levels and, depending on the candidate's expertise, undergraduate and graduate courses in Cybersecurity and/or Data Science, including service courses. Additional responsibilities include supervising student research and maintaining a computer engineering laboratory. Applicants should understand and be willing to support Seton Hall University's Catholic mission. Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related field is required and must be completed by the start date of employment. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarly research, and the mentorship of students through undergraduate and graduate research experiences. Desired Qualifications: Teaching experience and a record of scholarly publications are preferred. Salary Range: $98,625- $109,583 Exempt/Nonexempt: Exempt Physical Demands: General Office Environment Special Instructions to Applicants: Provide e-mail contact information for 3 references which may be contacted to provide recommendation letters. Provide a description of research goals Provide a diversity statement Benefits Information: Full Time Benefits Life today is complex. That’s why Seton Hall University offers a comprehensive package of benefits and programs to help you simplify and enrich your life. These benefits are important elements of your total university compensation package. Benefits include but are not limited to bundled medical, prescription, and vision insurance, dental insurance, and life insurance, and retirement plan. More information is available at https://www.shu.edu/human-resources/benefits.html . Seton Hall University is located in South Orange, New Jersey, 14 miles from New York City. It is the oldest Catholic diocesan institution of higher education in the United States and is home to about 6,300 undergraduate and 3,700 graduate students. A vibrant and culturally inclusive community, Seton Hall pursues academic excellence and ethical development in a collaborative environment and prepares its students to be servant leaders in their professional and community lives. Seton Hall University is an equal opportunity employer. It honors diverse perspectives and welcomes employees from all faith traditions. In turn, its employees respect Catholic beliefs and values, engage in servant leadership, and support the University’s mission as a Catholic institution of higher education. Advertised: 17 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "http://jobs.shu.edu/cw/en-us/job/497486/adjunct-professorenvironmental-studies": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor-Environmental Studies",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor-Environmental Studies Apply now Job no: 497486 Full time/Part time: Part-time Location: South Orange Categories: Faculty The Environmental Studies Program at Seton Hall University (https://www.shu.edu/academics/ba-environmental-studies.html) invites applications for an adjunct instructor of Environmental Studies for Spring 2027. The ideal candidate has an interdisciplinary background in the environmental social sciences or sustainability sciences, with both research and teaching experience. Applicants must be prepared to teach Introduction to Environmental Studies, our signature introductory survey course for both majors and non-majors. Seton Hall University is in South Orange, New Jersey, 14 miles from New York City. It is the oldest Catholic diocesan institution of higher education in the United States. It is home to approximately 6,300 undergraduate and 4,700 graduate students from all 50 states with alumni from more than 60 countries. An exciting and culturally diverse community, Seton Hall pursues academic excellence and ethical development in a collaborative environment and prepares its students to be servant leaders in their professional and community lives. Environmental Studies at Seton Hall is an interdisciplinary program in the College of Arts & Sciences that draws on faculty expertise in the natural sciences, social sciences, and humanities to study the complex relationships between humans and their environment. Students also learn by doing, with credit-bearing internships and other experiential learning opportunities. Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include teaching one 1000-level course (Introduction to Environmental Studies) during the Spring 2027 semester, with the possibility for renewal in future semesters. Required Qualifications: PhD in Environmental Studies, Sustainability Education, Environmental Policy, Geography, Anthropology, Sociology, or related fields. ABD candidates may be considered but the degree must be completed at the time of appointment. Salary Range: Minimum pay is $1230 per credit for those without a terminal degree and $1332.50 per credit for those with a terminal degree. Exempt/Nonexempt: Exempt Physical Demands: General Office Environment Special Instructions to Applicants: To Apply: Please submit a brief cover letter describing your relevant experience and teaching interests, along with a current CV and contact information for three references who can speak to your qualifications. Applicants are welcome, but not required, to include a sample syllabus, recent teaching evaluations, or other evidence of teaching effectiveness. Applications should be submitted prior to November 1, 2026, at which point review of applications will begin and will continue until the position is filled. For questions about the position, please contact Director of Environmental Studies, Dr. Jacob Weger. Benefits Information: Seton Hall University offers supplemental retirement benefits. Life today is complex. That’s why Seton Hall University offers a comprehensive package of benefits and programs to help you simplify and enrich your life. These benefits are important elements of your total university compensation package. Benefits include but are not limited to bundled medical, prescription, and vision insurance, dental insurance, and life insurance, and retirement plan. More information is available at https://www.shu.edu/human-resources/benefits.html . Seton Hall University is located in South Orange, New Jersey, 14 miles from New York City. It is the oldest Catholic diocesan institution of higher education in the United States and is home to about 6,300 undergraduate and 3,700 graduate students. A vibrant and culturally inclusive community, Seton Hall pursues academic excellence and ethical development in a collaborative environment and prepares its students to be servant leaders in their professional and community lives. Seton Hall University is an equal opportunity employer. It honors diverse perspectives and welcomes employees from all faith traditions. In turn, its employees respect Catholic beliefs and values, engage in servant leadership, and support the University’s mission as a Catholic institution of higher education. Advertised: 10 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "http://jobs.shu.edu/cw/en-us/job/497391/contract-faculty-department-of-physics": {
      "title": "Contract Faculty - Department of Physics",
      "description": "Contract Faculty - Department of Physics Apply now Job no: 497391 Full time/Part time: Full-time Location: South Orange Categories: Faculty The Department of Physics at Seton Hall University invites applications to fill a full-time contract teaching position beginning the Fall 2026 semester. A Ph.D. in Physics or related field is required. The candidate is expected to teach all levels of Physics courses. We seek a candidate who demonstrates excellence in teaching lectures and laboratory courses at all levels, especially to students of diverse backgrounds. Seton Hall University is located in South Orange, New Jersey, 14 miles from New York City. It is the oldest Catholic diocesan institution of higher education in the United States and is home to about 6,300 undergraduate and 4,700 graduate students. A vibrant and culturally diverse community, Seton Hall pursues academic excellence and ethical development in a collaborative environment and prepares its students to be servant leaders in their professional and community lives. Seton Hall University is an Equal Opportunity employer. It honors diversity and respects the religious commitments of all its employees. In turn, its employees respect Catholic beliefs and values, engage the Catholic Intellectual Tradition, and respect its mission as a Catholic institution of higher education. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching lecture and laboratory physics courses at all undergraduate and graduate levels. A total teaching load 12 credits/semester Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Physics or related field is required. Desired Qualifications: One or more years of teaching experience. Salary Range: $49,669-$55,188 Exempt/Nonexempt: Exempt Physical Demands: General Office Environment Special Instructions to Applicants: Benefits Information: Life today is complex. That’s why Seton Hall University offers a comprehensive package of benefits and programs to help you simplify and enrich your life. These benefits are important elements of your total university compensation package. Benefits include but are not limited to bundled medical, prescription, and vision insurance, dental insurance, and life insurance, and retirement plan. More information is available at https://www.shu.edu/human-resources/benefits.html . Seton Hall University is located in South Orange, New Jersey, 14 miles from New York City. It is the oldest Catholic diocesan institution of higher education in the United States and is home to about 6,300 undergraduate and 3,700 graduate students. A vibrant and culturally inclusive community, Seton Hall pursues academic excellence and ethical development in a collaborative environment and prepares its students to be servant leaders in their professional and community lives. Seton Hall University is an equal opportunity employer. It honors diverse perspectives and welcomes employees from all faith traditions. In turn, its employees respect Catholic beliefs and values, engage in servant leadership, and support the University’s mission as a Catholic institution of higher education. Advertised: 04 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
