      "title": "Adjunct Professor-Introduction to Ethics and Introduction to Biomedical Ethics",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor-Introduction to Ethics and Introduction to Biomedical Ethics Apply now Job no: 496477 Full time/Part time: Part-time Location: South Orange Categories: Faculty Adjunct professors for Introduction to Ethics and Introduction to Biomedical Ethics. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching the course and grading student work. Required Qualifications: MA in Philosophy minimum, Ph.D. preferred. Desired Qualifications: Ph.D. in Philosophy or closely related field Salary Range: Minimum pay is $1200 per credit for those without a terminal degree and $1300 per credit for those with a terminal degree Exempt/Nonexempt: Exempt Benefits Information: For details about employee benefits, see: https://www.shu.edu/human-resources/benefits.html Seton Hall University offers supplemental retirement benefits. Physical Demands: General Office Environment Special Instructions to Applicants: Seton Hall University is committed to programs of Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO). Advertised: 30 Aug 2024 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "http://jobs.shu.edu/cw/en-us/job/496202/adjunct-professor-information-technology-management": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Information Technology Management",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor - Information Technology Management Apply now Job no: 496202 Full time/Part time: Part-time Location: South Orange Categories: Faculty Department seeks IT professional to teach the required undergraduate introductory course in Information Technology. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach up to two sections of the required introductory course in IT. Each section will meet either twice per week for 75 minutes or once per week for 2.5 hours. Required Qualifications: Master's degree or higher in an IT related field or an MBA with work experience in IT. Desired Qualifications: Prior experience teaching courses in IT. Salary Range: Minimum pay is $1200 per credit for those without a terminal degree and $1300 per credit for those with a terminal degree Exempt/Nonexempt: Exempt Benefits Information: For details about employee benefits, see: https://www.shu.edu/human-resources/benefits.html Seton Hall University offers supplemental retirement benefits. Physical Demands: General Office Environment Special Instructions to Applicants: Seton Hall University is committed to programs of Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO). Advertised: 24 Apr 2024 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
